1
00:00:44,252 --> 00:00:47,964
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

2
00:01:25,543 --> 00:01:27,545
It didn't come out
nearly as pretty as I wanted.

3
00:01:32,801 --> 00:01:34,636
I should have gone with cursive,
shouldn't I?

4
00:01:36,513 --> 00:01:39,265
Well, at this point,
I think I did well enough.

5
00:01:51,486 --> 00:01:52,570
<i>Dr. Gye.</i>

6
00:01:53,404 --> 00:01:54,948
What exactly…

7
00:01:55,865 --> 00:01:57,283
are we looking at right now?

8
00:01:57,367 --> 00:01:59,369
D.N.

9
00:02:00,537 --> 00:02:01,996
We need photos.

10
00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:03,540
Sorry?

11
00:02:03,623 --> 00:02:04,958
Oh! Uh, okay.

12
00:02:06,751 --> 00:02:07,877
What's the problem?

13
00:02:08,461 --> 00:02:09,796
What is it? What's going on?

14
00:02:13,758 --> 00:02:15,135
What are you taking photos of?

15
00:02:24,435 --> 00:02:26,896
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

16
00:02:27,856 --> 00:02:30,066
EPISODE 5

17
00:02:31,151 --> 00:02:35,071
PHOTOS

18
00:02:39,742 --> 00:02:41,035
Dr. Gye, you came.

19
00:02:41,119 --> 00:02:45,999
Uh, all of his vital signs are currently
holding stable and he, um…

20
00:03:04,934 --> 00:03:08,188
It's getting awfully late, Dr. Gye.
I'm surprised to find you're still here.

21
00:03:10,190 --> 00:03:12,901
But you guys need to speak to the family.

22
00:03:15,028 --> 00:03:18,114
Uh, I think it'd be good if someone
spoke to the patient's family.

23
00:03:18,948 --> 00:03:19,949
Go ahead.

24
00:03:20,033 --> 00:03:22,160
W-Wait, me? But what do I say?

25
00:03:22,243 --> 00:03:24,662
"The surgery went great,
and he's asleep in the recovery ward.

26
00:03:24,746 --> 00:03:25,830
He'll be awake very shortly."

27
00:03:25,914 --> 00:03:28,458
Okay, but what do I say
about this? The, uh…

28
00:03:29,834 --> 00:03:30,960
Wait. What are you doing?

29
00:03:31,044 --> 00:03:33,796
Pass it to me, or I won't let you
come into any OR again.

30
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:35,215
Wait, I…

31
00:03:39,052 --> 00:03:41,054
WAITING ROOM

32
00:03:41,137 --> 00:03:42,472
Please sit, don't worry.

33
00:03:43,973 --> 00:03:48,186
Uh, Mr. Kwon's surgery went very well,
and he's now resting in the recovery room.

34
00:03:49,020 --> 00:03:51,439
Thank you, Doctor.
Thank you for saving his life.

35
00:03:51,522 --> 00:03:54,943
Uh, I was only assistant to Dr. Gye.
She was the primary surgeon.

36
00:03:55,026 --> 00:03:56,444
Oh!

37
00:03:58,655 --> 00:03:59,697
You saved him, Doctor.

38
00:04:06,079 --> 00:04:09,207
My mommy said to say thanks to you.

39
00:04:30,603 --> 00:04:32,146
<i>Thank you, Doctor.</i>

40
00:04:42,031 --> 00:04:46,202
Oh, here, sweet girl. Here. There you go.

41
00:04:46,286 --> 00:04:49,372
Mrs. Kwon, we'll monitor
Chung-hyeon for another half hour or so,

42
00:04:49,455 --> 00:04:52,208
and then he'll be moved from
the recovery room to the general ward.

43
00:04:52,292 --> 00:04:54,877
We'll let you know when that happens.
No need to worry too much.

44
00:04:54,961 --> 00:04:56,546
Okay. Thank you, Doctor.

45
00:04:56,629 --> 00:04:58,798
You must be exhausted.
Please, have a seat.

46
00:05:12,437 --> 00:05:13,604
<i>Asante.</i>

47
00:05:17,859 --> 00:05:22,488
Are you sure Mr. Kwon hasn't had any
surgery since the one performed by Dr. Na?

48
00:05:22,572 --> 00:05:24,741
Yes. I would have to do
some more research,

49
00:05:24,824 --> 00:05:26,659
but from what I found,
that looks to be right.

50
00:05:26,743 --> 00:05:28,244
I see.

51
00:05:29,245 --> 00:05:30,663
That's what we're up against, then.

52
00:05:31,706 --> 00:05:34,709
Uh, they're initials, right, Doctor?
I'm not the only one who sees it, right?

53
00:05:34,792 --> 00:05:36,586
- Looks like he carved--
- Stop talking about it.

54
00:05:36,669 --> 00:05:38,546
Or else I'll start to envision
how he did it.

55
00:05:40,631 --> 00:05:42,508
Oh, do you want
the pictures as well, Dr. Gye?

56
00:05:42,592 --> 00:05:43,760
And what are you going to do now?

57
00:05:43,843 --> 00:05:45,762
You're gonna tell Mr. Kwon
about it tomorrow, right?

58
00:05:45,845 --> 00:05:47,055
What are you, nuts?

59
00:05:47,138 --> 00:05:48,139
Well, shouldn't we tell him?

60
00:05:48,765 --> 00:05:50,767
Hey, why do you keep trying to run away?
This is serious.

61
00:05:51,267 --> 00:05:53,353
The agency is having a company dinner
and I don't want to be late.

62
00:05:53,436 --> 00:05:54,479
That's really what you're focusing on?

63
00:05:54,562 --> 00:05:56,773
Well, I need to hurry
or everyone will eat without me.

64
00:05:56,856 --> 00:05:58,649
You'll let the hospital know too, right?

65
00:05:58,733 --> 00:06:00,610
- No.
- You're not going to? Why?

66
00:06:00,693 --> 00:06:02,570
The hospital brought him in,
so why would I?

67
00:06:02,653 --> 00:06:04,113
Yeah, but the hospital also didn't know.

68
00:06:04,197 --> 00:06:06,449
You should tell them what's going on
and tell the patient directly too.

69
00:06:06,532 --> 00:06:07,700
Should he even know anything?

70
00:06:09,410 --> 00:06:11,621
- What?
- We're sure that'd be the right call?

71
00:06:13,873 --> 00:06:15,666
Uh, Dr. Jo, what exactly
are you trying to say?

72
00:06:15,750 --> 00:06:19,128
- Are you saying we should let this slide--
- As long as we never tell him about it,

73
00:06:19,212 --> 00:06:20,671
Kwon Chung-hyeon will carry on,
get discharged,

74
00:06:20,755 --> 00:06:23,508
and get to enjoy the rest of his life
with his wife and kids in peace.

75
00:06:23,591 --> 00:06:27,428
The only difference is that
he no longer has a gallbladder. That's it.

76
00:06:27,512 --> 00:06:29,472
All we have to tell is the usual,
watch your diet,

77
00:06:29,555 --> 00:06:32,058
cut back on drinking a little bit,
and get more exercise,

78
00:06:32,141 --> 00:06:33,142
Are you serious right now?

79
00:06:33,226 --> 00:06:35,812
You're shocked, scared, confused.
It's appalling that someone's this brutal,

80
00:06:35,895 --> 00:06:37,271
and I understand.

81
00:06:37,355 --> 00:06:40,024
It only looks that way to us
because we've seen that picture now.

82
00:06:41,109 --> 00:06:42,110
Just one.

83
00:06:42,944 --> 00:06:44,070
Just one more minute.

84
00:06:45,113 --> 00:06:46,989
A minute more
to think all this through again.

85
00:06:47,740 --> 00:06:50,368
And think about Kwon,
who still hasn't seen that picture yet.

86
00:06:53,121 --> 00:06:54,122
Hmm.

87
00:06:55,873 --> 00:06:57,625
Thanks for sharing
that insightful opinion.

88
00:06:58,251 --> 00:06:59,252
You tell the patient…

89
00:07:00,169 --> 00:07:01,504
and there's no way to go back.

90
00:07:05,550 --> 00:07:08,344
Anyone who's had surgery has the right
to know everything that happened.

91
00:07:08,428 --> 00:07:11,848
And it's a doctor's duty to disclose
anything that occurred during the surgery.

92
00:07:11,931 --> 00:07:12,932
I'll be going.

93
00:07:14,016 --> 00:07:16,185
Uh, but… Dr. Gye…

94
00:07:21,065 --> 00:07:23,067
Oh, damn.

95
00:07:27,363 --> 00:07:29,157
Dr. Jo, if we do what you suggest,

96
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:30,867
sure, he'll carry on living,

97
00:07:30,950 --> 00:07:32,410
except he'll never get any justice

98
00:07:32,493 --> 00:07:35,455
and go on praising the same person
who'd abused his body.

99
00:07:35,538 --> 00:07:38,583
I mean, are you saying
he should keep on doing surgeries

100
00:07:38,666 --> 00:07:41,127
and just go on disfiguring
other people, or what?

101
00:07:41,210 --> 00:07:43,838
Patients trust us to operate because
a doctor's not supposed to do this!

102
00:07:43,921 --> 00:07:45,214
You think I don't know that?

103
00:07:45,298 --> 00:07:47,675
The surgery was a success,
and he's not worried about anything.

104
00:07:47,758 --> 00:07:49,886
Is it on us to tell him about
the other surgery? Is it really?

105
00:07:49,969 --> 00:07:52,763
We saw what was in there!
I saw what he did to him.

106
00:07:53,639 --> 00:07:55,099
How could you just let this go?

107
00:07:55,183 --> 00:07:57,393
Just knowing that Na is still a doctor
when he's done something

108
00:07:57,477 --> 00:07:59,103
- so horribly vicious.
- Dr. Park, quit yelling!

109
00:08:01,022 --> 00:08:03,191
'Cause he's also a doctor,
are you covering for him in this?

110
00:08:05,568 --> 00:08:06,569
What?

111
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:11,073
Knowing what we know now…

112
00:08:12,408 --> 00:08:13,910
there's no going back on our side.

113
00:08:15,495 --> 00:08:17,163
How can we work with someone who would…

114
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:19,665
who would do anything that cruel?

115
00:08:36,849 --> 00:08:40,645
Let's get your socks on.
All right. Wanna put your socks on?

116
00:08:41,896 --> 00:08:42,897
Oh, wow, looks like someone

117
00:08:42,980 --> 00:08:44,941
- will need new shoes soon!
- I just couldn't.

118
00:08:45,024 --> 00:08:46,692
I couldn't bear to destroy their peace.

119
00:08:46,776 --> 00:08:47,818
Don't worry, honey.

120
00:08:47,902 --> 00:08:50,738
There's no hell worse
than knowing a tragedy you live with.

121
00:08:52,448 --> 00:08:54,700
Especially when it's heaven
all around you.

122
00:08:55,952 --> 00:08:56,953
Dr. Kim?

123
00:08:58,746 --> 00:08:59,956
Dr. Kim?

124
00:09:00,039 --> 00:09:01,958
- Dr. Kim.
- Huh? What?

125
00:09:02,542 --> 00:09:04,043
Okay, let's go.

126
00:09:04,126 --> 00:09:05,419
Let's go. Which bed is it?

127
00:09:05,503 --> 00:09:07,338
- Dressing, dressing…
- Dr. Kim.

128
00:09:07,421 --> 00:09:09,757
Oh, Dr. Na, when did you, uh…

129
00:09:10,424 --> 00:09:12,843
Ah, did you end up heading to the OR?

130
00:09:12,927 --> 00:09:14,595
I told you, you didn't have to come.

131
00:09:14,679 --> 00:09:16,597
I guess not, apparently. Nobody was there.

132
00:09:16,681 --> 00:09:19,725
Yeah, they finished the operation
and clocked out a while ago and went home.

133
00:09:19,809 --> 00:09:23,229
Well, I apologize. I would've gotten here
much earlier had I known--

134
00:09:23,312 --> 00:09:24,313
No, no, it's all right.

135
00:09:24,397 --> 00:09:25,982
Things were so hectic here.

136
00:09:26,065 --> 00:09:28,693
I was going to call, it's just…
there was a huge car accident rush.

137
00:09:28,776 --> 00:09:30,152
You must've hit bad traffic.

138
00:09:30,236 --> 00:09:31,279
Yeah, I did.

139
00:09:31,362 --> 00:09:33,239
That's actually the reason
I was here even later.

140
00:09:33,322 --> 00:09:35,199
Well, traffic should be better now,
so you should go home.

141
00:09:35,283 --> 00:09:37,618
Or you could end up in the OR
and be here all night.

142
00:09:40,705 --> 00:09:43,374
Oh, well, if you need
a pair of hands, then happily.

143
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:45,501
Oh, and…

144
00:09:46,961 --> 00:09:50,464
Did Doctor Gye Su-jeong, um,
perhaps give you a bit more detail?

145
00:09:51,048 --> 00:09:52,216
About?

146
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:56,053
Well, about the operation.
Or Kwon Chung-hyeon's condition, I guess?

147
00:10:09,817 --> 00:10:11,652
<i>Ah, I think some adhesions formed</i>

148
00:10:11,736 --> 00:10:14,113
<i>after the surgery you performed</i>
<i>during his military service.</i>

149
00:10:14,196 --> 00:10:15,656
<i>It is what it is.</i>

150
00:10:15,740 --> 00:10:19,535
<i>Since no one else was available, Dr. Gye</i>
<i>went into the OR with Park and Dr. Jo.</i>

151
00:10:20,036 --> 00:10:21,037
<i>I heard it went well.</i>

152
00:10:22,413 --> 00:10:23,539
I was curious about that.

153
00:10:25,916 --> 00:10:26,917
That's too bad.

154
00:10:33,507 --> 00:10:35,343
Oh, my goodness!

155
00:10:35,426 --> 00:10:37,720
Oh, my god, my mouth is watering.
This is incredible.

156
00:10:37,803 --> 00:10:39,472
Your face is all lit up! Look at you!

157
00:10:39,555 --> 00:10:40,556
Whoa!

158
00:10:42,767 --> 00:10:44,143
- There.
- All right.

159
00:10:44,226 --> 00:10:45,311
To getting money!

160
00:10:45,394 --> 00:10:46,937
- Cheers to that!
- Yeah, cheers to that!

161
00:10:51,233 --> 00:10:53,235
- Mmm!
- Ah!

162
00:10:55,571 --> 00:10:58,199
Once in a while,
I end up craving something like this.

163
00:10:58,282 --> 00:10:59,992
You need to eat
some real food now and again.

164
00:11:00,076 --> 00:11:02,244
Look at this. Is this a company dinner
or just a snack?

165
00:11:02,328 --> 00:11:03,829
Gosh, well, if you're so disappointed,

166
00:11:03,913 --> 00:11:06,290
get some more clients in the door,
Dr. Hua Tuo.

167
00:11:06,791 --> 00:11:09,293
I mean, you're just
scraping by right now, Eung-gu,

168
00:11:09,377 --> 00:11:12,880
'cause Dr. Mi-gyeong sends you patients
for acupuncture to manage their pain.

169
00:11:12,963 --> 00:11:15,549
Ah, you're slow to believe
in traditional Korean healing, aren't you?

170
00:11:15,633 --> 00:11:18,135
I sent you to a homeopathic clinic,
didn't I?

171
00:11:18,219 --> 00:11:19,220
That's traditional.

172
00:11:19,303 --> 00:11:21,597
They get car accident patients
and they're always short-staffed.

173
00:11:21,681 --> 00:11:24,100
Their direction doesn't match at all
with mine.

174
00:11:24,183 --> 00:11:26,811
Their direction doesn't matter.
What matters is you're saving lives.

175
00:11:26,894 --> 00:11:28,437
You mean,
"What matters is you're saving lives,

176
00:11:28,521 --> 00:11:30,231
and you're making dough."

177
00:11:32,108 --> 00:11:33,776
- Hey, I'm home.
- Here, sit, sit.

178
00:11:33,859 --> 00:11:34,860
- Come join us.
- Get ready!

179
00:11:34,944 --> 00:11:37,488
I made intestines and liver, sugar spiced!

180
00:11:37,571 --> 00:11:38,739
All the parts that you like!

181
00:11:38,823 --> 00:11:41,575
All right, all right.
There's <i>tteokbokki </i>there, too. Enjoy!

182
00:11:41,659 --> 00:11:42,660
My gosh!

183
00:11:42,743 --> 00:11:44,328
Hey, you…

184
00:11:44,412 --> 00:11:46,122
Good God, you eat a mile a minute.

185
00:11:46,205 --> 00:11:47,498
Hey, Su-jeong,

186
00:11:47,581 --> 00:11:49,583
this place makes a banging blood sausage.

187
00:11:49,667 --> 00:11:51,711
And, man, the liver?
Top tier, grade-A stuff.

188
00:11:51,794 --> 00:11:53,003
Your phone's going off like crazy!

189
00:11:55,965 --> 00:11:58,134
You should take it.
It could be an emergency surgery.

190
00:12:05,766 --> 00:12:08,561
<i>Dr. Gye, I'm sending you</i>
<i>the pictures, just in case.</i>

191
00:12:08,644 --> 00:12:09,687
<i>You probably don't want to see them,</i>

192
00:12:09,770 --> 00:12:12,690
<i>but you should have them for when</i>
<i>you talk to the patient tomorrow.</i>

193
00:12:12,773 --> 00:12:15,151
<i>But are you really not gonna</i>
<i>tell the hospital about this?</i>

194
00:12:15,234 --> 00:12:17,236
<i>I saw everything. I'll back you up.</i>

195
00:12:17,319 --> 00:12:19,822
<i>Can I take your silence</i>
<i>to mean you're still thinking it over?</i>

196
00:12:19,905 --> 00:12:23,075
<i>It really bothers you too, right, Dr. Gye?</i>
<i>Right? Right? Right?</i>

197
00:12:23,159 --> 00:12:24,952
<i>Tell you what,</i>
<i>if you don't want to answer,</i>

198
00:12:25,035 --> 00:12:26,495
<i>you can just send back a "Y" or an "N."</i>

199
00:12:26,579 --> 00:12:28,748
Anyone know how to block someone?

200
00:12:36,630 --> 00:12:39,592
Ladies, starting today,
I won't be eating liver.

201
00:12:39,675 --> 00:12:41,635
You're a doctor.
How are you squeamish with organs?

202
00:12:41,719 --> 00:12:44,472
When does a doctor of traditional
medicine see human organs?

203
00:12:44,555 --> 00:12:46,432
Holy crap, how could he
do something so awful?

204
00:12:46,515 --> 00:12:47,767
This is good.

205
00:12:48,350 --> 00:12:51,604
- I wish they served this at the hospital.
- Oh, come on, Su-jeong…

206
00:12:51,687 --> 00:12:52,813
All right.

207
00:12:53,731 --> 00:12:55,024
Whatever's put on your--

208
00:12:55,107 --> 00:12:56,192
I told you, didn't I?

209
00:12:56,275 --> 00:12:58,903
When I shook his hand,
his fishy smell rubbed off.

210
00:13:00,279 --> 00:13:04,283
Ah, well, I have a meeting with
Director Bu soon, so I better make a note.

211
00:13:07,620 --> 00:13:08,621
Give me the photos.

212
00:13:11,665 --> 00:13:12,666
Send them to me.

213
00:13:14,335 --> 00:13:16,754
You stop right there!
Answer me, young lady!

214
00:13:16,837 --> 00:13:19,048
Hey, at least give your auntie
a little reply here, will you?

215
00:13:19,131 --> 00:13:20,633
She's up to no good.

216
00:13:20,716 --> 00:13:24,178
This emergency thing, for Su-jeong
could be a bit mundane, don't you think?

217
00:13:25,387 --> 00:13:26,430
Well, that's true.

218
00:13:27,848 --> 00:13:29,141
Ugh, I can't get a break.

219
00:13:51,956 --> 00:13:53,749
"Dae-il Na."

220
00:13:54,250 --> 00:13:55,376
"Dr. Na."

221
00:14:00,548 --> 00:14:03,217
Just as I thought.
This was his first time.

222
00:14:03,801 --> 00:14:06,428
He couldn't manage his strength
at that point,

223
00:14:06,512 --> 00:14:08,389
so it came out uneven and crude.

224
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:19,775
LAW

225
00:14:23,654 --> 00:14:25,990
Let's finish up quickly.

226
00:14:26,615 --> 00:14:27,616
What time is it?

227
00:14:41,881 --> 00:14:43,215
We should sharpen our blades.

228
00:14:43,299 --> 00:14:46,677
Otherwise, the cuts
end up looking like scribbles.

229
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:49,346
We're going to spread them
all over the place.

230
00:14:49,430 --> 00:14:53,017
The moment people see it,
it'll etch fear of us into their minds.

231
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:56,562
We need to carve them like scribbles
to make it more chilling.

232
00:15:05,070 --> 00:15:07,698
A medical volunteer for the insurgents?

233
00:15:07,781 --> 00:15:11,035
Why not join us
as a Russian mercenary instead?

234
00:15:11,535 --> 00:15:15,372
If our commander doesn't pull through,
we'll carve it into you too.

235
00:15:16,498 --> 00:15:20,336
And your colleagues
and the other insurgent bastards.

236
00:15:21,253 --> 00:15:23,422
She doesn't understand you.

237
00:15:23,505 --> 00:15:26,091
She hasn't said a word. Must be scared.

238
00:15:26,175 --> 00:15:28,469
At least she didn't piss her pants.

239
00:15:35,267 --> 00:15:37,269
Better keep your blade sharp.

240
00:15:37,937 --> 00:15:38,938
What?

241
00:15:39,772 --> 00:15:41,732
It's your turn next.

242
00:15:42,691 --> 00:15:43,692
Ow!

243
00:15:44,693 --> 00:15:47,154
How long do I have to keep
waking you up like this, huh?

244
00:15:47,237 --> 00:15:49,657
- Hmm?
- Huh? Are those eyes still shut?

245
00:15:53,702 --> 00:15:57,623
Oh, man, how do you wake me up
at just the right time?

246
00:15:57,706 --> 00:15:58,707
- Here.
- Oh!

247
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:03,003
By the way, what's this
"You're next. You're next" thing about?

248
00:16:03,087 --> 00:16:04,088
My goodness.

249
00:16:04,171 --> 00:16:06,423
If your dream was about that incident,

250
00:16:07,174 --> 00:16:08,592
just forget it.

251
00:16:25,985 --> 00:16:28,988
- Have you eaten yet?
- Yes. A big lunch, actually.

252
00:16:29,947 --> 00:16:32,825
There has been great feedback
for other doctors as well,

253
00:16:32,908 --> 00:16:35,577
but Dr. Na has been getting
quite a lot of praise I hear.

254
00:16:35,661 --> 00:16:37,913
- Mm-hmm.
- Countering the negative views

255
00:16:37,997 --> 00:16:42,001
in regards to us recently,
Dr. Na is different. That is clear.

256
00:16:42,084 --> 00:16:44,670
Impressive. He hasn't even
worked here long.

257
00:16:44,753 --> 00:16:47,923
Mr. Chairman, you've got a good eye.

258
00:16:48,007 --> 00:16:50,384
"I was thoroughly comforted
with his encouraging attitude,

259
00:16:50,467 --> 00:16:52,553
"thoughtful explanation
and warm demeanor."

260
00:16:52,636 --> 00:16:55,389
I do wonder how other doctors
have been treating their patients

261
00:16:55,472 --> 00:16:56,724
for them to show such gratitude.

262
00:16:56,807 --> 00:16:59,059
God, there you go with this shit again.

263
00:17:00,227 --> 00:17:02,396
It's fair to say
you brought in a good doctor.

264
00:17:02,479 --> 00:17:04,189
Take it as a good thing, just for now.

265
00:17:04,273 --> 00:17:05,983
Oh, but… Uh-oh.

266
00:17:06,066 --> 00:17:08,902
Wow, this hospital
is really showing its age.

267
00:17:08,986 --> 00:17:11,405
It looks exactly the same
as when I worked here.

268
00:17:11,488 --> 00:17:13,741
Uh, on that note, actually, Mr. Mayor,
regarding the city's initiative

269
00:17:13,824 --> 00:17:15,492
you're working on for medical welfare…

270
00:17:15,576 --> 00:17:16,910
Hey, don't you have anything to eat here?

271
00:17:16,994 --> 00:17:19,955
You could only scrape together
a cup of coffee? Really? Hey!

272
00:17:31,008 --> 00:17:33,844
<i>Pay us what you owe,</i>
<i>or I'll sue your pants off.</i>

273
00:17:34,344 --> 00:17:35,721
<i>I'll leave the melon for you.</i>

274
00:17:35,804 --> 00:17:37,598
I'm sure you'll be calling me soon.

275
00:17:38,974 --> 00:17:40,934
Why is he standing there
with the fridge door open?

276
00:17:41,018 --> 00:17:42,436
My goodness.

277
00:17:48,192 --> 00:17:50,110
MOM, DAD

278
00:17:54,281 --> 00:17:57,659
This is mine? You saw this in there?
Are you sure?

279
00:17:58,577 --> 00:18:01,622
Um, in most cases,
a liver injury such as this

280
00:18:01,705 --> 00:18:05,793
would only leave a faint scar,
or heal entirely within a week or less.

281
00:18:07,086 --> 00:18:09,171
Uh, then how would this be in there?

282
00:18:10,839 --> 00:18:13,509
I mean, I haven't had a surgery recently.

283
00:18:13,592 --> 00:18:16,428
Uh, this is a rather rare case,
where extreme adhesions near the injury

284
00:18:16,512 --> 00:18:20,307
were actually working as preservation,
as it was enclosed by the serosa.

285
00:18:20,390 --> 00:18:22,309
I'm sorry, but I'm not understanding.

286
00:18:23,977 --> 00:18:24,978
Uh…

287
00:18:26,188 --> 00:18:29,399
Wait a minute. So, back then…

288
00:18:31,443 --> 00:18:33,362
Oh! Baseball!

289
00:18:33,445 --> 00:18:35,697
You've got pay-per-view in here! Jackpot!

290
00:18:37,491 --> 00:18:38,700
Listen, Doctor,

291
00:18:38,784 --> 00:18:41,495
I know you struggle to deal
with these kinds of things,

292
00:18:41,578 --> 00:18:43,622
but throwing a game on right now
is a bit much, don't you think?

293
00:18:43,705 --> 00:18:44,706
DAD

294
00:18:44,790 --> 00:18:47,501
So, what you're saying is it's cool
to watch the other channels, or…

295
00:18:49,753 --> 00:18:51,713
Well…

296
00:18:52,422 --> 00:18:55,551
the operation you underwent 15 years ago
was the last operation you had--

297
00:18:55,634 --> 00:18:57,177
Thank you for doing so great
with my surgery.

298
00:18:58,303 --> 00:18:59,388
I'm very blessed.

299
00:18:59,471 --> 00:19:01,515
I pushed it off for too long
because of work.

300
00:19:03,350 --> 00:19:05,644
Thank goodness you were here,
Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

301
00:19:06,353 --> 00:19:07,980
I swear I'll repay you one day.

302
00:19:09,898 --> 00:19:13,277
Uh, and things were hectic
with the huge traffic accident that day.

303
00:19:14,153 --> 00:19:16,530
I really thought
I was going to die, I'll tell you that.

304
00:19:17,156 --> 00:19:20,033
As opposed to pushing it,
I should've done it quick, right?

305
00:19:22,327 --> 00:19:24,830
Then it'd have been Dr. Na
who would've handled your surgery.

306
00:19:25,622 --> 00:19:28,542
There's no record of you having
any operation under anesthesia,

307
00:19:28,625 --> 00:19:31,879
before or after the surgery Dr. Na
performed during your military service.

308
00:19:32,963 --> 00:19:35,549
Dr. Na did this horrible thing!
He's the one who--

309
00:19:43,599 --> 00:19:44,892
Daddy!

310
00:19:46,810 --> 00:19:48,103
Throw it to me here!

311
00:19:48,187 --> 00:19:50,105
Whoa, and he makes the catch!

312
00:19:50,189 --> 00:19:53,233
- It's your ball now!
- Okay, let's go play outside, huh?

313
00:19:53,317 --> 00:19:54,860
- Daddy!
- Okay.

314
00:19:56,695 --> 00:19:59,865
Uh, since your recovery is the most
important thing right now,

315
00:19:59,948 --> 00:20:01,950
please ensure you rest plenty
and drink lots of fluids.

316
00:20:02,034 --> 00:20:03,911
Next month, my wife's
having A-rin's sibling.

317
00:20:06,413 --> 00:20:08,290
She's really looking forward
to meeting them.

318
00:20:08,874 --> 00:20:11,043
She was born in this hospital,
so will the new one.

319
00:20:11,126 --> 00:20:14,087
There won't be any negative outcomes
or retaliations for speaking up.

320
00:20:18,884 --> 00:20:20,510
That was his price for saving my life,
I guess.

321
00:20:24,556 --> 00:20:25,849
Kwon Chung-hyeon…

322
00:20:28,352 --> 00:20:29,728
We'll let it stay in the past.

323
00:20:33,607 --> 00:20:35,651
- Sir, I just can't--
- All right, then that's what we'll do.

324
00:20:38,737 --> 00:20:41,740
Mr. Kwon, you said that your wife
plans to give birth in this hospital,

325
00:20:41,823 --> 00:20:43,992
but your house is quite far from here.

326
00:20:44,076 --> 00:20:45,994
You've chosen this hospital specifically…

327
00:20:48,038 --> 00:20:49,665
since you're often here on work.

328
00:20:55,254 --> 00:20:57,130
Maybe you've seen
quite a few people lose their jobs

329
00:20:57,214 --> 00:20:59,549
over issues like this
because they've reported it too.

330
00:20:59,633 --> 00:21:01,343
But, Dr. Gye, I…

331
00:21:06,431 --> 00:21:08,475
So just live your life
like nothing happened.

332
00:21:08,976 --> 00:21:10,352
You have that option.

333
00:21:11,019 --> 00:21:14,314
And you're allowed to.
Nobody's going to judge you for moving on.

334
00:21:24,992 --> 00:21:26,285
Okay, close your eyes.

335
00:21:27,661 --> 00:21:30,163
Now, open up and follow
my finger with your eyes.

336
00:21:34,584 --> 00:21:36,044
<i>I'm good at playing dumb.</i>

337
00:21:40,590 --> 00:21:43,802
<i>That's how, despite my lack of</i>
<i>a fancy degree or connections,</i>

338
00:21:43,885 --> 00:21:45,095
<i>I made it this far.</i>

339
00:21:50,475 --> 00:21:51,518
ANESTHESIA RECORD
KWON CHUNG-HYEON

340
00:21:59,443 --> 00:22:00,944
<i>And I'll continue to be good at it.</i>

341
00:22:08,660 --> 00:22:10,537
- I need to talk with you.
- No thank you.

342
00:22:10,620 --> 00:22:12,789
- I'd love to talk too.
- Wasn't asking you.

343
00:22:12,873 --> 00:22:15,334
I fell like you're excluding me.
I'm used to it.

344
00:22:15,417 --> 00:22:17,252
That said, have a look at this.

345
00:22:18,086 --> 00:22:19,796
Here, take that, give it a read.

346
00:22:19,880 --> 00:22:22,174
"Emergency Department
Violence Response Manual," huh?

347
00:22:22,257 --> 00:22:24,551
Check it out.
We're reviewing it next week.

348
00:22:24,634 --> 00:22:26,970
- Come by and learn!
- I have surgery then.

349
00:22:27,054 --> 00:22:29,639
- Still, put it in your calendar.
- This is really good.

350
00:22:30,932 --> 00:22:33,852
Hey, so somebody snuck in
and took all our lounge snacks today.

351
00:22:33,935 --> 00:22:35,812
Not just any thief. It was a master thief.

352
00:22:35,896 --> 00:22:37,814
Is this what it's like
to get hit with a burglary?

353
00:22:38,565 --> 00:22:40,275
Hold on, they cleared us out?

354
00:22:40,359 --> 00:22:42,402
So, you're saying there's no more snacks?

355
00:22:42,486 --> 00:22:44,237
No, there still are.
You're holding them now.

356
00:22:45,697 --> 00:22:47,032
No, but they cleared it all out?

357
00:22:47,115 --> 00:22:50,410
Yeah. That dirty thief ate everything,
so that's all we have left.

358
00:22:51,495 --> 00:22:52,746
No way.

359
00:22:52,829 --> 00:22:53,872
Who could it be?

360
00:22:53,955 --> 00:22:55,957
Hey!

361
00:22:56,041 --> 00:22:57,125
Hey, Jo Won-jin!

362
00:22:57,209 --> 00:22:58,919
- Hey, Dr. Jo!
- Hey! My snacks!

363
00:22:59,002 --> 00:23:00,921
Where are you going?
Keep your issues upstairs.

364
00:23:01,004 --> 00:23:03,090
Why cause problems when
we're just trying to keep the peace here!

365
00:23:03,173 --> 00:23:04,633
I'm anxious!

366
00:23:05,258 --> 00:23:06,802
I'll come to the review though! For…

367
00:23:10,806 --> 00:23:13,183
Oh, shit!
Ugh, God, what are you, a sprinter?

368
00:23:14,267 --> 00:23:16,520
What did you write in your record
for Kwon's surgery?

369
00:23:16,603 --> 00:23:17,604
I just wrote it.

370
00:23:17,687 --> 00:23:19,481
- I've been struggling to do it.
- Well, I hope you finished.

371
00:23:19,564 --> 00:23:21,358
- Damn it!
- Oh, no. No, wait!

372
00:23:22,067 --> 00:23:25,153
- Give it back! Oh!
- Mmm!

373
00:23:25,862 --> 00:23:27,322
It was almost empty anyways.

374
00:23:29,950 --> 00:23:31,535
What did you do?

375
00:23:33,245 --> 00:23:34,496
It's all I can focus on.

376
00:23:36,456 --> 00:23:37,791
Since it's all you can focus on,

377
00:23:39,334 --> 00:23:41,711
then go buy some for yourself.
You've got plenty of money.

378
00:23:41,795 --> 00:23:43,422
Don't you turn this back around.

379
00:23:44,548 --> 00:23:47,426
Look, I thought I could do it,
I genuinely tried, I just can't do it.

380
00:23:47,509 --> 00:23:50,011
Sure, I can write one up as if
nothing happened. I guess I could.

381
00:23:50,095 --> 00:23:51,096
Okay, so go ahead and do that.

382
00:23:51,179 --> 00:23:52,806
Well, it happened
and I can't pretend nothing's wrong.

383
00:23:55,100 --> 00:23:56,309
Well, if it makes it easier…

384
00:23:57,477 --> 00:23:59,563
think about what you said to me before.

385
00:24:00,397 --> 00:24:02,023
"Think this through again
from Kwon's perspective."

386
00:24:02,107 --> 00:24:04,609
Doesn't this…
Doesn't this bother you at all?

387
00:24:07,863 --> 00:24:08,989
I feel horrible.

388
00:24:09,865 --> 00:24:11,158
Actually really shitty.

389
00:24:12,993 --> 00:24:15,579
Hey! It's emergency Dr. Gye!

390
00:24:20,417 --> 00:24:22,085
You two are together a lot.

391
00:24:23,336 --> 00:24:24,546
You don't look too busy in GS.

392
00:24:24,629 --> 00:24:25,839
We're busier than ever.

393
00:24:26,465 --> 00:24:27,841
We're so busy that, unfortunately,

394
00:24:27,924 --> 00:24:30,552
we couldn't make it back here
fast enough at that time.

395
00:24:30,635 --> 00:24:32,554
How'd you know to be
at the hospital at that time?

396
00:24:32,637 --> 00:24:34,389
It's like you knew Kwon would be here.

397
00:24:34,973 --> 00:24:38,435
Not "like I knew." I actually did know.

398
00:24:40,520 --> 00:24:43,023
We knew. 'Cause anyone would've
showed up if something's that bad.

399
00:24:43,106 --> 00:24:44,107
Anyone would've come in.

400
00:24:44,191 --> 00:24:47,068
Or it'll turn into a major surgery
'cause they took too long to get here.

401
00:24:47,152 --> 00:24:49,696
Oh! Were you wanting it
to turn into a major surgery?

402
00:24:49,779 --> 00:24:51,656
- Uh…
- That's ridiculous.

403
00:24:51,740 --> 00:24:53,450
Why are you picking a fight with her?

404
00:24:54,618 --> 00:24:56,620
Seems you're missing the eldest
of you three boneheads.

405
00:24:56,703 --> 00:24:59,039
Uh, he's with Dr. Na right now
in Mr. Kwon's room.

406
00:24:59,122 --> 00:25:00,123
Oh!

407
00:25:01,833 --> 00:25:02,834
Visiting him.

408
00:25:10,091 --> 00:25:13,845
I think you should just stay here. This is
a two-person room, not just a single.

409
00:25:13,929 --> 00:25:15,096
Too crowded in the ones for six.

410
00:25:15,180 --> 00:25:16,681
I think I'll go home, actually.

411
00:25:16,765 --> 00:25:19,100
Imposing on you here
is the last thing I'd want to do.

412
00:25:19,184 --> 00:25:21,019
I wasn't even able to do your surgery.

413
00:25:21,102 --> 00:25:23,438
The bed next to you will be
empty for a while, just stay here.

414
00:25:24,105 --> 00:25:25,106
I think I'm all right.

415
00:25:25,607 --> 00:25:27,234
Thank you both for checking on me though.

416
00:25:27,317 --> 00:25:28,860
I know you're so busy.

417
00:25:28,944 --> 00:25:31,947
What pharmaceutical rep
gets treated this amazingly, right?

418
00:25:32,030 --> 00:25:35,575
Oh, if we counted the drinks we've
had together, they'd stack into the sky.

419
00:25:35,659 --> 00:25:38,745
But, hey, recover soon. We've gotta
continue working and golfing again.

420
00:25:39,329 --> 00:25:40,622
Sure thing. You bet.

421
00:25:41,915 --> 00:25:45,377
Dr. Na was absolutely shattered
he wasn't there to do your operation.

422
00:25:46,211 --> 00:25:48,129
Had Dr. Na done your surgery,

423
00:25:48,213 --> 00:25:50,882
it would've been a kind of special moment
only doctors can experience.

424
00:25:51,550 --> 00:25:53,635
That moment during surgery
when he sees your liver

425
00:25:53,718 --> 00:25:55,887
- right next to your gall bladder.
- Come on. That's enough.

426
00:25:56,805 --> 00:25:58,014
A-rin, here, sweetie.

427
00:25:58,098 --> 00:26:00,600
Let's help daddy's ouchy heal
and blow a little air on it.

428
00:26:02,936 --> 00:26:04,145
Hey!

429
00:26:04,229 --> 00:26:05,981
Get away from him. He's my patient.

430
00:26:06,064 --> 00:26:08,775
Oh, well, I think there's been
a misunderstanding.

431
00:26:08,858 --> 00:26:10,652
I wasn't trying to do anything unusual.

432
00:26:10,735 --> 00:26:12,320
Dr. Do, excuse me.

433
00:26:12,404 --> 00:26:14,781
- Dr. Bae and Dr. Ma are looking for you.
- Okay.

434
00:26:15,365 --> 00:26:16,616
Dr. Do, the conference.

435
00:26:16,700 --> 00:26:18,577
Oh, that's right.
Mr. Kwon, I'll see you again later.

436
00:26:18,660 --> 00:26:20,203
- Sure.
- Dr. Na, let's go.

437
00:26:21,037 --> 00:26:23,665
- See you later, A-rin.
- Bye-bye.

438
00:26:53,028 --> 00:26:54,029
Are you angry?

439
00:26:55,363 --> 00:26:57,282
I thought about it.
I see why you misunderstood.

440
00:26:58,617 --> 00:26:59,618
My fault.

441
00:27:01,369 --> 00:27:03,496
Before I have to go to the conference,

442
00:27:03,580 --> 00:27:06,166
I wanna ask when
you might be free for a meal?

443
00:27:06,249 --> 00:27:09,294
I'd like to show my gratitude
for how much you helped out Mr. Kwon,

444
00:27:09,377 --> 00:27:10,629
and also…

445
00:27:13,048 --> 00:27:14,049
How'd the surgery go?

446
00:27:22,390 --> 00:27:24,976
As usual, only surgery
will get you to look at me.

447
00:27:26,227 --> 00:27:27,896
I heard the adhesions were severe.

448
00:27:27,979 --> 00:27:30,106
It must've been from his previous surgery.

449
00:27:31,024 --> 00:27:32,484
Well, thank you for your help.

450
00:27:35,403 --> 00:27:37,656
So, how did it look? Tidy?

451
00:27:47,582 --> 00:27:50,126
It was shoddy work, done crudely.

452
00:27:51,127 --> 00:27:53,672
Maybe it was your first time
performing that operation?

453
00:27:53,755 --> 00:27:57,133
Hmm. Don't hold back.

454
00:27:57,759 --> 00:28:00,428
Uh, I was in such a rush back then,
I could barely think straight.

455
00:28:00,970 --> 00:28:04,432
But nonetheless, it's not like
he'd ever know it was there,

456
00:28:04,516 --> 00:28:06,768
or, at that point,
anybody else would either.

457
00:28:06,851 --> 00:28:08,395
Like it hurts him at all.

458
00:28:08,978 --> 00:28:10,814
He's alive, thanks to me.

459
00:28:10,897 --> 00:28:13,274
Now he has a family, a good career.

460
00:28:14,734 --> 00:28:15,944
Sounds pretty lucky, actually.

461
00:28:17,362 --> 00:28:20,407
But, I can understand how shoddy
the surgery that I performed

462
00:28:20,490 --> 00:28:22,534
over-- well, now over a decade ago,

463
00:28:23,118 --> 00:28:24,661
could look at present.

464
00:28:24,744 --> 00:28:26,162
Being honest…

465
00:28:27,038 --> 00:28:29,582
it's really quite embarrassing.

466
00:28:31,084 --> 00:28:32,544
So, how about dinner tomorrow?

467
00:28:36,131 --> 00:28:38,341
To be honest, Doctor,
I wish you hadn't said that.

468
00:28:39,300 --> 00:28:40,301
What?

469
00:28:43,680 --> 00:28:46,391
Dumb, boneheaded thought
that he's alive thanks to you.

470
00:28:47,767 --> 00:28:49,728
Now I have to call in a favor
with Ms. Jang.

471
00:28:54,566 --> 00:28:57,235
Oh, I'm sure that
you're ready to be discharged.

472
00:28:57,318 --> 00:29:00,363
- Oh! Hi there.
- The doctor who did your surgery.

473
00:29:00,447 --> 00:29:03,283
Oh! Doctor, it's nice to meet you.

474
00:29:03,366 --> 00:29:05,410
Oh, thank you so much.

475
00:29:05,493 --> 00:29:07,203
Oh, you're right, goodness.

476
00:29:07,287 --> 00:29:09,831
- She'll need help opening it.
- Oh, thank you so much.

477
00:29:11,124 --> 00:29:12,542
Dr. Gye is the reason
why she's still here.

478
00:29:13,209 --> 00:29:16,129
Everyone else said it seemed impossible,
but it wasn't to her.

479
00:29:16,212 --> 00:29:19,466
I saw the video of the surgery.
I was so shocked watching.

480
00:29:20,175 --> 00:29:21,676
She got it all done so fast.

481
00:29:23,344 --> 00:29:25,638
The first time Dr. Gye spoke to me,
she asked a question.

482
00:29:28,683 --> 00:29:29,726
What was it?

483
00:29:32,812 --> 00:29:33,855
"You also a doctor?"

484
00:29:46,075 --> 00:29:47,827
You're doing well.

485
00:29:47,911 --> 00:29:50,121
- Wow! You're so sweet.
- Thank you for everything, Doctor.

486
00:29:50,205 --> 00:29:51,831
Are you doing all right?

487
00:29:51,915 --> 00:29:53,333
Yes, thank you both.

488
00:29:53,416 --> 00:29:55,043
We're so grateful for you, Doctor.

489
00:29:55,126 --> 00:29:57,629
- She can be discharged, right?
- That'd be great.

490
00:30:11,601 --> 00:30:12,602
<i>I'm gonna save you.</i>

491
00:30:13,645 --> 00:30:15,021
No matter what, I'll save you.

492
00:30:15,688 --> 00:30:16,689
<i>Thank you, Dr. Na.</i>

493
00:30:16,773 --> 00:30:18,483
- How cute.
- Thank you for everything, Doctor.

494
00:30:18,566 --> 00:30:20,235
How precious.
She looks just like your wife.

495
00:30:20,318 --> 00:30:21,319
- She really does.
- Yes.

496
00:30:21,402 --> 00:30:23,238
Thank god she didn't get her dad's looks.

497
00:30:23,321 --> 00:30:25,156
Let's help daddy's ouchy heal
and blow a little air on it.

498
00:30:25,240 --> 00:30:26,241
Just a minute.

499
00:31:26,217 --> 00:31:27,218
What is it?

500
00:31:34,434 --> 00:31:35,685
I don't feel anything.

501
00:31:51,576 --> 00:31:53,494
What?

502
00:31:53,578 --> 00:31:54,746
Damn it.

503
00:31:57,081 --> 00:31:59,000
Freaking hand.

504
00:32:00,376 --> 00:32:01,502
Oh.

505
00:32:02,879 --> 00:32:05,757
- You couldn't have done this in there?
- Long while since it's bothered you.

506
00:32:06,507 --> 00:32:08,760
Well, then stop reaching for a drink
the second it starts bugging you.

507
00:32:08,843 --> 00:32:11,012
That's what's causing it.

508
00:32:11,554 --> 00:32:12,805
Ah!

509
00:32:12,889 --> 00:32:14,140
<i>Let's see what you can do.</i>

510
00:32:14,223 --> 00:32:15,892
Huh, God, come on Su-jeong.

511
00:32:15,975 --> 00:32:17,352
This is gonna be trouble all right.

512
00:32:18,186 --> 00:32:20,271
I think we'll need to pull out
all the stops for this.

513
00:32:21,439 --> 00:32:25,443
Eung-gu, take these needles out of me,
I'm shaking again already. You damn quack.

514
00:32:27,070 --> 00:32:29,656
Our famously irresistible Ma Seong-gu.

515
00:32:30,239 --> 00:32:32,283
- Now, appe's a cakewalk to you.
- Mmm!

516
00:32:35,411 --> 00:32:38,498
Dr. Jo Won-jin, is that a nod of approval
I see there?

517
00:32:39,624 --> 00:32:41,376
I think she's got
something else on her mind.

518
00:32:44,003 --> 00:32:46,172
Sorry, just, um, feeling kind of tired.

519
00:32:46,756 --> 00:32:48,466
Schedule's packed, isn't it?

520
00:32:48,549 --> 00:32:49,550
Well, yeah, I guess so.

521
00:32:50,259 --> 00:32:52,428
We really need to get more people
coming in next year.

522
00:32:52,512 --> 00:32:54,222
Sure, yeah, for surgeries.

523
00:32:54,847 --> 00:32:57,141
It's a good we've got Dr. Na Dae-il
on our team, huh?

524
00:33:06,943 --> 00:33:08,069
Oh…

525
00:33:08,152 --> 00:33:09,654
Doctor, you came here in person?

526
00:33:10,405 --> 00:33:12,907
Where… Where did they go?

527
00:33:15,159 --> 00:33:17,870
"I'm going out to grab dinner
at that budae-jjigae place

528
00:33:17,954 --> 00:33:19,455
where you fainted. Kiss kiss."

529
00:33:19,539 --> 00:33:20,581
Heart.

530
00:33:21,332 --> 00:33:24,460
- May I look?
- Oh, yeah.

531
00:33:32,468 --> 00:33:33,970
What, Doctor? How's it looking?

532
00:33:34,679 --> 00:33:36,806
Is-- Is something wrong with it?

533
00:33:37,598 --> 00:33:38,599
Sit up.

534
00:33:52,530 --> 00:33:54,032
DAD

535
00:34:01,414 --> 00:34:02,415
Oh.

536
00:34:22,101 --> 00:34:25,229
I used to take his kids to kindergarten.

537
00:34:26,022 --> 00:34:27,732
Other doctors' kids.

538
00:34:27,815 --> 00:34:29,525
I don't even know where
my own kid's daycare is,

539
00:34:29,609 --> 00:34:31,069
much less actually bring her there.

540
00:34:38,076 --> 00:34:40,036
And now she already knows how to write.

541
00:34:44,415 --> 00:34:46,000
It's like yesterday, she was tiny.

542
00:34:49,629 --> 00:34:51,297
Why'd you show me that picture, Doctor,

543
00:34:51,380 --> 00:34:53,341
when there's absolutely nothing
I can do about it.

544
00:34:53,925 --> 00:34:56,427
It's not like I'll die from it.
I can't see it with my own eyes.

545
00:34:57,178 --> 00:34:59,055
I mean, no one else would know
if I stay quiet.

546
00:35:02,975 --> 00:35:05,770
I'd say, that the person who etched
those letters thought the same as you.

547
00:35:07,480 --> 00:35:08,481
Doctor,

548
00:35:09,774 --> 00:35:10,775
truthfully…

549
00:35:12,944 --> 00:35:14,070
I can see plenty clearly.

550
00:35:16,114 --> 00:35:17,240
Every time I look at myself.

551
00:35:19,033 --> 00:35:20,034
Like a toy for him.

552
00:35:21,869 --> 00:35:24,789
I see how he literally treated my body
like a toy for him to play with.

553
00:35:24,872 --> 00:35:26,165
And after seeing him today…

554
00:35:28,000 --> 00:35:30,086
I think he came round to seeing that too,
and that…

555
00:35:31,671 --> 00:35:33,840
That's what's driving me insane right now.

556
00:35:36,801 --> 00:35:41,097
And that is what that asshole who did this
wanted to see over everything.

557
00:35:53,442 --> 00:35:54,485
JANG HUI-SUK

558
00:35:54,569 --> 00:35:57,530
<i>I'm taking it out of your pay.</i>
<i>I'll get every last penny.</i>

559
00:35:57,613 --> 00:35:58,865
NA DAE-IL
HEALTH SCREENING RESULTS

560
00:36:02,869 --> 00:36:04,370
HEALTH SCREENING REPORT

561
00:36:08,416 --> 00:36:11,294
By the way, Dr. Na went on leave.

562
00:36:11,377 --> 00:36:13,087
That's weird, he barely just started.

563
00:36:13,171 --> 00:36:15,131
When he took the job,
they had to do a physical on him.

564
00:36:15,214 --> 00:36:16,883
I guess a spot on his liver turned up.

565
00:36:16,966 --> 00:36:20,595
He'll need a biopsy,
but how are they going to get it?

566
00:36:21,387 --> 00:36:23,931
He'll be off for quite a long time,
it's open surgery.

567
00:36:25,016 --> 00:36:26,017
Who'll be his surgeon?

568
00:36:29,812 --> 00:36:30,813
It can get pretty boring here.

569
00:36:31,647 --> 00:36:33,733
There's sports on channel 32.

570
00:36:43,743 --> 00:36:45,912
Better keep your blade sharp.

571
00:36:45,995 --> 00:36:47,580
It's your turn next.

572
00:36:51,042 --> 00:36:53,961
TEN DAYS LATER

573
00:36:55,338 --> 00:36:58,132
Ah! As expected, you woke up quickly.

574
00:36:58,216 --> 00:37:00,343
Welcome back. Your surgery went well.

575
00:37:00,426 --> 00:37:01,427
Thank you, Doctor.

576
00:37:02,261 --> 00:37:03,262
Huh?

577
00:37:04,013 --> 00:37:05,389
- I said thank you.
- Oh!

578
00:37:05,973 --> 00:37:07,642
It's a pleasure. There was nothing to it.

579
00:37:08,976 --> 00:37:09,977
Make sure to get plenty of rest.

580
00:37:10,728 --> 00:37:11,729
See you.

581
00:37:18,402 --> 00:37:22,156
It just happened to be between the
hepatic vein and inferior vena cava, so…

582
00:37:23,699 --> 00:37:25,576
Here, eat up.
The food's actually pretty good.

583
00:37:25,660 --> 00:37:26,911
Okay, thanks.

584
00:37:26,994 --> 00:37:28,829
Soon you'll be back on your feet again.

585
00:37:28,913 --> 00:37:32,625
Oh, speaking of, I'm thinking of walking
over to the CCTV archive room to watch it.

586
00:37:32,708 --> 00:37:34,418
Oh, to review the tape of your surgery?

587
00:37:35,086 --> 00:37:37,046
I know that it was
just an ordinary operation,

588
00:37:37,880 --> 00:37:39,090
but I do want to watch it.

589
00:37:39,173 --> 00:37:41,676
What the hell for?
Are you really that perverted?

590
00:37:41,759 --> 00:37:44,428
No, it's just that I'm curious.

591
00:37:44,512 --> 00:37:46,180
Hmm, is that all right?

592
00:37:47,682 --> 00:37:49,350
For Dr. Na, it should be fine.

593
00:37:50,184 --> 00:37:51,227
Why wouldn't it?

594
00:37:51,310 --> 00:37:53,145
You know, the cameras in the OR,
they can see.

595
00:37:53,229 --> 00:37:55,314
When those cameras first went up,
we all protested it.

596
00:37:55,940 --> 00:37:58,901
Eventually, we became required
to have them in there as a legal thing.

597
00:37:58,985 --> 00:38:01,195
I don't understand why they would
pass that kind of law.

598
00:38:01,279 --> 00:38:02,571
Leave my surgeries alone.

599
00:38:02,655 --> 00:38:05,700
But we managed to twist
the language around a bit to…

600
00:38:05,783 --> 00:38:07,868
make the footage
impossible to access. See?

601
00:38:07,952 --> 00:38:11,831
Uh, you don't know this
since you were a military doctor.

602
00:38:13,416 --> 00:38:15,209
- Well, what now?
- Uh, you need

603
00:38:15,293 --> 00:38:18,045
consent from everyone who was in the OR
to watch the video.

604
00:38:18,129 --> 00:38:21,424
The PAs, the surgeon, even the
anesthesiologist needs to sign off.

605
00:38:21,507 --> 00:38:25,511
In other words, it's next to impossible
for a patient to watch the video.

606
00:38:26,595 --> 00:38:29,557
But I'm relatively certain
Dr. Mun Yeong-jong would show it to you.

607
00:38:29,640 --> 00:38:31,267
Of course! Definitely!

608
00:38:32,101 --> 00:38:34,812
Now I can say that I know
how a patient feels.

609
00:38:34,895 --> 00:38:36,605
Hey, now don't you start being crazy.

610
00:38:36,689 --> 00:38:39,150
Doctors are always doctors,
even when they're sick.

611
00:38:39,233 --> 00:38:40,234
Is that what you really think?

612
00:38:40,818 --> 00:38:43,529
What do you want, Snake Su-jeong?
What are you doing here?

613
00:38:43,612 --> 00:38:45,197
Thanks for checking in on me.

614
00:38:58,627 --> 00:39:00,379
Uh. What's happening?

615
00:39:02,673 --> 00:39:03,924
They must have gotten together.

616
00:39:15,019 --> 00:39:16,479
Really?

617
00:39:17,646 --> 00:39:18,773
D.N.

618
00:39:18,856 --> 00:39:19,857
Whoa, whoa, whoa! What--

619
00:39:19,940 --> 00:39:23,569
Well, it's… I gotta tell you…

620
00:39:24,487 --> 00:39:26,072
That could be difficult.

621
00:39:26,155 --> 00:39:27,990
But, please, Doctor,
why can't you just show it to me?

622
00:39:28,074 --> 00:39:30,910
Well, look. If I give you my consent
just because you're a fellow doctor,

623
00:39:30,993 --> 00:39:32,244
it wouldn't be fair to the other patients.

624
00:39:32,328 --> 00:39:34,455
Doctor, come on, it's me, Dae-il.

625
00:39:35,414 --> 00:39:36,415
Is it about trust?

626
00:39:37,666 --> 00:39:39,085
Is it something you're hiding from me?

627
00:39:39,168 --> 00:39:40,169
Hey.

628
00:39:41,128 --> 00:39:43,464
You shouldn't go around
making accusations like this.

629
00:39:43,547 --> 00:39:46,384
Did you die in there? Huh?
Do you suspect malpractice?

630
00:39:46,467 --> 00:39:48,135
But then why are you hiding the surgery?

631
00:39:49,136 --> 00:39:52,765
The procedure went fine.
My god, it was just a quick surgery.

632
00:39:52,848 --> 00:39:55,393
Then why won't you show me the video?
I mean, what's the issue?

633
00:39:57,186 --> 00:39:59,188
- I think you're hiding something from me.
- Listen…

634
00:40:01,649 --> 00:40:03,692
I went golfing with a friend
before the surgery.

635
00:40:04,318 --> 00:40:05,319
And I…

636
00:40:06,737 --> 00:40:08,781
won the round. So…

637
00:40:08,864 --> 00:40:10,032
Who did you go with?

638
00:40:10,658 --> 00:40:12,535
Our friend the drug peddler.

639
00:40:13,327 --> 00:40:14,328
He was discharged.

640
00:40:15,079 --> 00:40:17,706
He was making the rounds with the guys
to celebrate his recovery.

641
00:40:18,749 --> 00:40:19,750
But did you…

642
00:40:20,835 --> 00:40:21,919
Yeah, I had a drink.

643
00:40:22,753 --> 00:40:23,754
Then two drinks.

644
00:40:24,505 --> 00:40:26,173
- Okay, so…
- Then three drinks.

645
00:40:29,009 --> 00:40:30,386
You weren't handling the surgery?

646
00:40:32,179 --> 00:40:33,347
Who did the operation then?

647
00:40:34,056 --> 00:40:35,057
Are you crazy?

648
00:40:35,724 --> 00:40:37,977
Do we need to start breathalyzing
doctors in the OR now?

649
00:40:38,060 --> 00:40:40,646
For the love of God,
how dare you speak to me like that!

650
00:40:40,729 --> 00:40:43,232
What, you think you're in charge of my OR?

651
00:40:43,315 --> 00:40:44,942
Are you the one doing the surgery?

652
00:40:45,693 --> 00:40:46,694
No, you're not.

653
00:40:46,777 --> 00:40:49,363
Then why are you wasting my time
with this stunt you're pulling?

654
00:40:49,447 --> 00:40:51,699
- Get out of the way! Move!
- I can't do that.

655
00:40:51,782 --> 00:40:53,200
I can't let you in there like this.

656
00:40:53,284 --> 00:40:54,827
What if I make you?

657
00:40:54,910 --> 00:40:56,745
Jesus Christ! Fine.

658
00:40:56,829 --> 00:40:58,789
We can just all get contaminated.

659
00:40:58,873 --> 00:41:00,040
Take a shot!

660
00:41:00,124 --> 00:41:01,292
Take it! Hit a girl!

661
00:41:01,375 --> 00:41:02,626
Please tell me you're kidding.

662
00:41:04,712 --> 00:41:06,005
What moron would do that?

663
00:41:06,589 --> 00:41:07,590
I apologize.

664
00:41:08,757 --> 00:41:11,469
Look, Director, this broad is crazy.

665
00:41:11,552 --> 00:41:13,387
I told you, if you showed up
impaired to an operation,

666
00:41:13,471 --> 00:41:16,348
I would call a disciplinary hearing.
Did I or did I not?

667
00:41:17,766 --> 00:41:20,686
If you do that,
there won't be anyone here to operate.

668
00:41:20,769 --> 00:41:22,062
- Come on.
- We would have plenty.

669
00:41:22,688 --> 00:41:25,566
What's more, they aren't insane drunks.

670
00:41:25,649 --> 00:41:27,401
I heard you like touching nurse's butts
while you operate,

671
00:41:27,485 --> 00:41:28,611
pretending you didn't mean to.

672
00:41:28,694 --> 00:41:30,738
Well, that's just an old tradition I got.

673
00:41:30,821 --> 00:41:32,114
It's just something to bring good luck.

674
00:41:32,198 --> 00:41:33,866
Good luck? Jesus!

675
00:41:34,617 --> 00:41:35,826
That's not something a doctor would say.

676
00:41:35,910 --> 00:41:36,952
Watch your mouth!

677
00:41:37,036 --> 00:41:40,873
Dr. Jo Won-jin, if you want to
file a complaint with the hospital,

678
00:41:40,956 --> 00:41:43,292
document your case in writing
and send it in.

679
00:41:43,375 --> 00:41:44,877
It's not your place to start a fight.

680
00:41:45,836 --> 00:41:47,254
Get back to the OR right now.

681
00:41:52,676 --> 00:41:57,139
Man, someone like her has no idea
the burden of the scalpel in your hands.

682
00:41:58,516 --> 00:42:00,684
Thousands of people whose whole existence

683
00:42:00,768 --> 00:42:03,771
relies entirely on these hands.

684
00:42:03,854 --> 00:42:06,273
Talking is not the answer here.

685
00:42:06,357 --> 00:42:07,399
What?

686
00:42:08,984 --> 00:42:09,985
Says you.

687
00:42:10,569 --> 00:42:12,821
This tradition and burden,
do you hear yourself?

688
00:42:14,323 --> 00:42:15,324
Mun Yeong-jong.

689
00:42:16,867 --> 00:42:19,703
I've been a scalpel jockey
since the days you were still in training.

690
00:42:19,787 --> 00:42:23,123
Do you think you are talking to some
battered, used-up troglodyte?

691
00:42:30,297 --> 00:42:31,715
Get a hold of the ethics committee.

692
00:42:31,799 --> 00:42:34,718
Fine then. Do it. Oh, you go ahead.

693
00:42:37,721 --> 00:42:41,225
How many surgeries
are on my board for today?

694
00:42:41,308 --> 00:42:44,019
And also, how many surgeons
are ready in GS?

695
00:42:47,189 --> 00:42:49,650
All right then,
put her in number four, please.

696
00:42:53,153 --> 00:42:54,154
Okay, so…

697
00:42:59,326 --> 00:43:01,412
- Okay, so…
- Tell me.

698
00:43:04,498 --> 00:43:05,583
Who did the surgery?

699
00:43:19,638 --> 00:43:20,639
I'm Gye Su-jeong.

700
00:43:21,515 --> 00:43:23,684
Get ready, and let's begin the surgery.

701
00:43:27,605 --> 00:43:29,982
<i>I will give consent for you</i>
<i>to view the OR footage,</i>

702
00:43:30,065 --> 00:43:31,775
<i>since, on paper, I'm the primary surgeon.</i>

703
00:43:32,484 --> 00:43:34,445
<i>Look, I'm trying to stop</i>
<i>a disciplinary hearing</i>

704
00:43:34,528 --> 00:43:36,113
<i>from being called</i>
<i>with Magnolia, all right?</i>

705
00:43:36,196 --> 00:43:38,073
<i>So maybe you should let this slide too.</i>

706
00:43:55,424 --> 00:43:56,425
Hold on…

707
00:43:57,343 --> 00:43:59,011
What's going on here?

708
00:43:59,094 --> 00:44:03,140
Oh, that day the ER Violence
Control Protocol was activated as a drill.

709
00:44:03,223 --> 00:44:05,351
You're seeing when the siren went off.

710
00:44:05,434 --> 00:44:07,019
I think they were just a bit surprised.

711
00:44:07,936 --> 00:44:10,230
Right here. Can you zoom in here?

712
00:44:11,273 --> 00:44:13,359
They blocked that control.
We can't get closer.

713
00:44:13,442 --> 00:44:15,110
- They blocked that control?
- That's right.

714
00:44:15,194 --> 00:44:16,904
The doctors, when they had it configured,

715
00:44:16,987 --> 00:44:19,490
put the camera there
to catch the widest angle possible

716
00:44:19,573 --> 00:44:21,116
and disabled the zoom function.

717
00:44:27,748 --> 00:44:28,749
I swear to…

718
00:44:30,000 --> 00:44:31,293
Those crazy sons of bitches!

719
00:45:01,490 --> 00:45:03,283
The fried chicken at this place is killer!

720
00:45:04,535 --> 00:45:08,122
Ah, so this is where our Su-jeong
is working nowadays?

721
00:45:08,622 --> 00:45:09,998
I guess it's really been a while.

722
00:45:10,082 --> 00:45:11,583
I'm very proud of her, I must say.

723
00:45:11,667 --> 00:45:13,669
I was worried she might be
too broken to function.

724
00:45:15,129 --> 00:45:17,005
Here we are. Hello, Doctor, how are you?

725
00:45:17,089 --> 00:45:18,841
- Hey there.
- Is Dr. Gye Su-jeong here right now?

726
00:45:19,967 --> 00:45:21,927
Ah! You're her director and family,
aren't you?

727
00:45:22,010 --> 00:45:25,264
Oh! Oh, my! Well, Dr. Gye
must have told you about who I am.

728
00:45:25,347 --> 00:45:26,890
Oh, Dr. Gye, not so much.

729
00:45:26,974 --> 00:45:28,350
Ah, but he did!

730
00:45:28,434 --> 00:45:30,686
- Hey! Our intern doctor. Good to see you.
- Hello. How are you?

731
00:45:31,395 --> 00:45:34,148
Uh, the dinner, would you also
like me to come? Can I join as well?

732
00:45:34,231 --> 00:45:35,441
Of course, come along.

733
00:45:35,524 --> 00:45:38,736
We always plan for another two guests
to attend our agency dinners.

734
00:45:38,819 --> 00:45:41,363
Oh, so it's an agency dinner?
So, does two guests mean…

735
00:45:41,447 --> 00:45:42,906
- Are you asking that I--
- Hello, Ms. Jang.

736
00:45:43,949 --> 00:45:46,326
Um, I'm Dr. Jo Won-jin.

737
00:45:46,410 --> 00:45:48,412
I didn't expect to tag along
for your dinner tonight.

738
00:45:48,495 --> 00:45:49,830
Ah, okay. So not invited, got it.

739
00:45:50,831 --> 00:45:53,625
We're not doing anything fancy.
Just some beer and chicken like usual.

740
00:45:54,293 --> 00:45:57,755
Just our thanks for the politeness
you've shown while working with Dr. Gye.

741
00:45:57,838 --> 00:45:59,965
Oh, is she busy right now?
I don't see her anywhere.

742
00:46:00,048 --> 00:46:02,801
She was just doing
a burn dressing earlier, on that side.

743
00:46:03,719 --> 00:46:05,637
Wait, isn't that Dr. Na Dae-il?

744
00:46:06,513 --> 00:46:07,556
What's he doing?

745
00:46:07,639 --> 00:46:09,683
I chose the right day
to do this company dinner.

746
00:46:11,435 --> 00:46:13,937
Hey, Dr. Na, hold on. What's going on?
This is the ER--

747
00:46:14,021 --> 00:46:15,063
Where the hell is Gye Su-jeong?

748
00:46:15,856 --> 00:46:16,899
Whoa, what kind of language is that?

749
00:46:16,982 --> 00:46:19,526
- Where is she, your teacher? Huh?
- Whoa!

750
00:46:19,610 --> 00:46:21,153
I never taught that kid.

751
00:46:23,197 --> 00:46:25,282
No matter how well I might've
stitched you up earlier,

752
00:46:25,365 --> 00:46:27,451
- you should be resting right now.
- What are you doing?

753
00:46:27,534 --> 00:46:28,869
- Whoa! What the hell?
- Hey!

754
00:46:30,454 --> 00:46:32,998
Keep that up and you'll end up
seeing your own organs.

755
00:46:38,879 --> 00:46:40,631
What did you pull in that surgery?

756
00:46:42,174 --> 00:46:43,967
Don't worry, it's not like it hurts.

757
00:46:44,051 --> 00:46:46,011
or that anybody else
would ever know it was there,

758
00:46:46,094 --> 00:46:49,306
or that you would know
it was there, right?

759
00:46:56,772 --> 00:46:57,773
Don't tell me

760
00:46:58,482 --> 00:46:59,483
you did that?

761
00:47:00,651 --> 00:47:02,653
It'll be gone in a week,
so why are you crying?

762
00:47:03,987 --> 00:47:05,280
I'm sorry, what?

763
00:47:05,364 --> 00:47:07,658
I don't think you'll get to
experience the same miracle

764
00:47:07,741 --> 00:47:10,035
where ten years down the road
it hasn't healed a bit.

765
00:47:12,746 --> 00:47:13,747
Ah.

766
00:47:15,082 --> 00:47:16,291
Well, let's say that happened.

767
00:47:19,878 --> 00:47:20,921
How would you know

768
00:47:22,005 --> 00:47:23,590
if I did carve my initials inside you?

769
00:47:30,764 --> 00:47:31,765
Gye Su-jeong, you little…

770
00:47:38,105 --> 00:47:40,107
Damn it!

771
00:47:49,199 --> 00:47:50,701
Gye Su-jeong!

772
00:47:51,410 --> 00:47:52,661
Watch out!

773
00:47:52,744 --> 00:47:54,121
Yes, hello?

774
00:47:54,204 --> 00:47:57,082
This is the ER at Guseo University
Medical Center, please come quick!

775
00:48:03,672 --> 00:48:04,882
Dr. Gye, wait!

776
00:48:13,515 --> 00:48:15,392
Dr. Gye! What the--

777
00:48:16,268 --> 00:48:17,644
Dr. Gye, you're bleeding.

778
00:48:17,728 --> 00:48:19,479
We've got to stop it!
You have be able to do surgeries!

779
00:48:19,563 --> 00:48:21,690
Stop it. It's not my hand, don't worry.

780
00:48:21,773 --> 00:48:24,985
Oh, yeah? Then your hand will be up next.

781
00:48:26,486 --> 00:48:28,322
Hey!

782
00:48:29,323 --> 00:48:30,324
You there, nut job!

783
00:48:30,407 --> 00:48:33,118
You just screwed with
the star of my brand new agency

784
00:48:33,201 --> 00:48:34,912
and our highest earning cash cow!

785
00:48:34,995 --> 00:48:37,372
Ms. Jang, what are you doing?
The police are on their way.

786
00:48:37,456 --> 00:48:40,417
She's the one getting food on our table,
do you understand?

787
00:48:40,500 --> 00:48:43,503
The one that's buying beer and chicken
at our dinner tonight!

788
00:48:43,587 --> 00:48:44,588
Wait, really?

789
00:48:45,714 --> 00:48:48,967
Okay, to hell with all this. Looks like
I have to come teach you a lesson!

790
00:48:49,051 --> 00:48:51,261
What are you saying, you old witch?

791
00:48:53,972 --> 00:48:55,933
- Oh, no!
- Ah!

792
00:48:56,725 --> 00:48:57,893
Oh, shit! My God!

793
00:49:03,440 --> 00:49:04,441
Oh! Oh!

794
00:49:05,525 --> 00:49:08,320
Oh!

795
00:49:43,355 --> 00:49:44,648
Don't move big guy.

796
00:49:45,232 --> 00:49:46,733
You feel a pinch in your neck, right?

797
00:49:47,776 --> 00:49:50,696
Think I was only out there saving lives
when I was up in North Korea?

798
00:49:52,489 --> 00:49:56,743
Do you think, while keeping my folks fed,
that healing was all I did?

799
00:49:56,827 --> 00:49:58,704
No one will ever know…

800
00:49:58,787 --> 00:50:00,664
- Are you okay?
- …why you became a bumbling vegetable.

801
00:50:00,747 --> 00:50:02,374
- I really need to say something to you.
- Well?

802
00:50:02,457 --> 00:50:03,834
You wanna see what that's like?

803
00:50:09,965 --> 00:50:12,259
Looks like you're totally screwed.

804
00:50:14,302 --> 00:50:17,264
I refuse to take that patient.
That would-be killer. Okay?

805
00:50:17,347 --> 00:50:18,682
You know I don't turn patients down here,

806
00:50:18,765 --> 00:50:21,268
but that one has to be transferred
no matter what, okay?

807
00:50:21,351 --> 00:50:23,437
- How could a doctor do that?
- Are you okay?

808
00:50:23,520 --> 00:50:26,690
I don't understand how Dr. Na Dae-il
could do such a brutal, reckless thing.

809
00:50:27,899 --> 00:50:29,818
Oh, Dr. Gye, the blood.

810
00:50:34,364 --> 00:50:36,867
Damn, Dr. Park, are you okay?

811
00:50:36,950 --> 00:50:38,285
You planned all this, didn't you?

812
00:50:39,036 --> 00:50:41,246
What is this supposed to be?
Omelet rice? Ketchup?

813
00:50:41,329 --> 00:50:42,706
What the hell is going on over there?

814
00:50:42,789 --> 00:50:44,332
Gye Su-jeong is whispering
something to him.

815
00:50:44,416 --> 00:50:45,959
Guess no one knew she was crazy, huh?

816
00:50:54,426 --> 00:50:55,552
Gye Su-jeong!

817
00:50:55,635 --> 00:50:58,138
- Good lord!
- Hey, Gye Su-jeong is hurt.

818
00:50:58,221 --> 00:51:00,140
- What?
- Her arm was cut open.

819
00:51:00,223 --> 00:51:01,224
Oh, she's bleeding.

820
00:51:02,309 --> 00:51:04,144
- Looks like it needs stitches.
- Get her into trauma.

821
00:51:04,227 --> 00:51:07,189
Dr. Gye Su-jeong causes trouble
regardless of the floor she's on.

822
00:51:08,440 --> 00:51:09,483
Looks like the time…

823
00:51:11,026 --> 00:51:13,320
truly has come to terminate the contract.

824
00:51:13,403 --> 00:51:16,448
I would take a peek at that.

825
00:51:17,115 --> 00:51:19,868
I told you you'd get a notice
slapped on you, didn't I?

826
00:51:23,955 --> 00:51:25,582
Shall they come seize your property now?

827
00:51:32,589 --> 00:51:34,841
Just the skin, simple.

828
00:51:35,425 --> 00:51:36,635
Yeah, right? Nice and easy.

829
00:51:37,177 --> 00:51:39,805
- One simple suture.
- So, um, who's going to…

830
00:51:40,430 --> 00:51:43,934
<i>If you need stitches in your arm </i>

831
00:51:44,017 --> 00:51:47,020
<i>The answer's clearly Tae-gyeong </i>

832
00:51:47,104 --> 00:51:48,647
Everyone seems pretty excited around here.

833
00:51:48,730 --> 00:51:50,941
It's not fair if you do it. Not alone.

834
00:51:51,024 --> 00:51:53,068
I was hoping I'd also be able
to stitch up Gye's arm.

835
00:51:53,151 --> 00:51:55,403
- Why? What?
- Why?

836
00:51:56,154 --> 00:51:57,864
'Cause I've gone through a lot
'cause of Dr. Gye,

837
00:51:57,948 --> 00:52:01,284
so I guess I've been planning on
making it hurt a little.

838
00:52:01,368 --> 00:52:03,245
Oh, so I'm not the only one here
that was thinking that?

839
00:52:03,328 --> 00:52:05,539
I'm overcome with a strange desire
to put some stitches--

840
00:52:05,622 --> 00:52:07,624
This is actually really mean, you guys.
Seriously.

841
00:52:07,707 --> 00:52:11,086
Dr. Gye's arm isn't made of iron.
Just look at it, it's a human arm.

842
00:52:11,169 --> 00:52:13,421
I'm the reason you got hurt, so should I--

843
00:52:13,505 --> 00:52:15,382
Winner gets to do the stitches.
Rock, paper, scissors! Go!

844
00:52:15,465 --> 00:52:16,508
Stop!

845
00:52:17,342 --> 00:52:18,677
I want…

846
00:52:28,270 --> 00:52:29,437
you to suture me.

847
00:52:30,480 --> 00:52:31,898
You're asking that I do it?

848
00:52:31,982 --> 00:52:34,484
- That's not--
- Dr. Gye, that seems very bold and risky.

849
00:52:34,568 --> 00:52:36,319
I mean, really, are you sure?

850
00:52:36,403 --> 00:52:38,572
I'm genuinely worried about you
for the first time, Dr. Gye.

851
00:52:38,655 --> 00:52:41,074
Plus it could actually
aggravate your wound.

852
00:52:41,158 --> 00:52:42,325
I'll stitch her up then.

853
00:52:42,409 --> 00:52:43,410
No!

854
00:52:44,202 --> 00:52:47,330
- Then, with that…
- Rock, paper, scissors!

855
00:52:47,414 --> 00:52:48,915
- I didn't lose.
- Darn it!

856
00:52:48,999 --> 00:52:50,792
Will you get out!

857
00:53:09,477 --> 00:53:12,397
Is there any pain?
Are you doing all right there, Doctor?

858
00:53:12,480 --> 00:53:14,858
Shut up and I'll be all right
when you're done.

859
00:53:21,198 --> 00:53:22,449
Oh.

860
00:53:25,493 --> 00:53:27,662
It's all good.
Starting is half the battle, really.

861
00:53:29,748 --> 00:53:32,751
Somebody will finish the other half
of those sutures, I suppose.

862
00:53:32,834 --> 00:53:35,420
You know the next rotation, right?
It's soon isn't it?

863
00:53:35,503 --> 00:53:37,214
Huh? Huh? God, I'm so anxious right now.

864
00:53:37,297 --> 00:53:39,341
Good lord, that arm
is still attached to somebody.

865
00:53:40,342 --> 00:53:42,719
Look, little doctor, it's still
not too late for you to change to

866
00:53:42,802 --> 00:53:45,180
- traditional Korean medicine and explore…
- Let's go.

867
00:53:45,847 --> 00:53:48,266
- But he's got the face of traditional--
- Let's go!

868
00:53:48,350 --> 00:53:49,476
Why do you always do this?

869
00:54:04,241 --> 00:54:05,325
Oh, my God!

870
00:54:07,619 --> 00:54:08,620
SURGERY PERSONNEL CHANGES

871
00:54:08,703 --> 00:54:12,332
"Na Dae-il.
Suspension from position and dismissal."

872
00:54:12,415 --> 00:54:16,211
Oh, gosh, Dr. Na Dae-il.
Oh, God, why'd you have to do that?

873
00:54:16,294 --> 00:54:18,838
- I heard he's getting arrested.
- Seriously?

874
00:54:22,759 --> 00:54:24,010
Hey!

875
00:54:24,636 --> 00:54:26,012
- Oh!
- Mr. Kwon!

876
00:54:27,389 --> 00:54:30,225
- Look at you! Oh, thank you, thank you.
- Here you go.

877
00:54:30,308 --> 00:54:31,393
How have you been feeling?

878
00:54:31,476 --> 00:54:34,562
Sorry, a major incident occurred here,
so I couldn't check in with you.

879
00:54:34,646 --> 00:54:36,231
I appreciate your consideration.

880
00:54:36,314 --> 00:54:38,108
Now I'm feeling all ready to play.

881
00:54:38,775 --> 00:54:41,486
I got the papers you sent
for the new drug. I read through them.

882
00:54:41,569 --> 00:54:43,613
- Are you ready to go?
- Uh…

883
00:54:44,447 --> 00:54:46,491
You know what happened
with Dr. Na Dae-il recently?

884
00:54:47,200 --> 00:54:50,161
Can I ask, why'd he do it?
I just figured you'd know, that's all.

885
00:54:50,245 --> 00:54:52,414
- Uh…
- You know?

886
00:54:52,497 --> 00:54:54,624
Oh, well, how would I know?

887
00:54:54,708 --> 00:54:56,710
I was shocked by
the news as well, of course.

888
00:54:56,793 --> 00:54:58,086
- Oh.
- Really?

889
00:55:18,356 --> 00:55:20,734
I mean, after the surgery,
did anything in particular…

890
00:55:20,817 --> 00:55:22,485
- Hello, Doctors!
- Oh, hey!

891
00:55:25,780 --> 00:55:28,074
What are you doing?
Why are you wiping the desk?

892
00:55:34,831 --> 00:55:37,500
There we go. See you later. See you later.

893
00:55:37,584 --> 00:55:40,503
What… What did you just leave over there?

894
00:55:42,797 --> 00:55:43,798
Dr. Do, um…

895
00:55:46,509 --> 00:55:47,802
I think you'll want to see this.

896
00:55:57,645 --> 00:55:59,314
APPOINTMENT
GENERAL SURGERY LOCUM, DR. GYE SU-JEONG

897
00:55:59,397 --> 00:56:00,815
Oh, man.

898
00:56:04,778 --> 00:56:07,572
Dr. Gye Su-jeong! Here! Here, here.

899
00:56:08,490 --> 00:56:11,117
They just got this ready,
so I picked it up for you.

900
00:56:12,577 --> 00:56:14,120
Come on, don't you want to put it on?

901
00:56:18,666 --> 00:56:19,667
I can take that.

902
00:56:31,012 --> 00:56:33,348
<i>This is the story of a lone wolf.</i>

903
00:56:35,016 --> 00:56:38,353
To think the esteemed Director Bu
would come all this way in person.

904
00:56:39,437 --> 00:56:41,856
You sued me for aggravated assault
and disorderly conduct,

905
00:56:41,940 --> 00:56:43,691
so I figured that would've
been enough for you.

906
00:56:43,775 --> 00:56:45,610
But it doesn't appear that's the case.

907
00:56:45,693 --> 00:56:48,738
Ms. Jang recently sent along
a certain picture.

908
00:56:48,822 --> 00:56:50,407
She wanted to negotiate.

909
00:56:50,490 --> 00:56:51,658
Thanks to your handiwork,

910
00:56:52,242 --> 00:56:55,036
I had to reinstate Dr. Gye's position
in general surgery again.

911
00:56:55,995 --> 00:56:58,498
<i>A solitary figure</i>
<i>who emerged from the dark</i>

912
00:56:58,581 --> 00:57:00,834
<i>in the era of the mafia in white,</i>

913
00:57:00,917 --> 00:57:05,130
<i>an age in which the practice of medicine</i>
<i>is driven by money and power.</i>

914
00:57:07,382 --> 00:57:09,342
<i>She belongs to no group.</i>

915
00:57:11,344 --> 00:57:13,888
Do you want to know why I did what I did?

916
00:57:14,389 --> 00:57:15,390
Not really.

917
00:57:15,473 --> 00:57:17,892
I actually don't care. I really don't.

918
00:57:18,476 --> 00:57:22,105
Though, I will say I was quite surprised.

919
00:57:22,188 --> 00:57:24,732
How is it that, through all these years,

920
00:57:24,816 --> 00:57:27,652
that wound still remained
as clear as it did?

921
00:57:28,695 --> 00:57:31,614
My, isn't the human body marvelous?

922
00:57:32,365 --> 00:57:36,077
A doctor cannot afford to capitulate
to boredom, drop their guard.

923
00:57:36,995 --> 00:57:39,873
I've realized that being a doctor means

924
00:57:39,956 --> 00:57:43,084
learning through your patients' bodies
to get a deeper understanding,

925
00:57:45,044 --> 00:57:47,297
not seek your own enjoyment in the act.

926
00:57:51,426 --> 00:57:54,929
You really think I hadn't predicted
he'd keep quiet on what I did?

927
00:57:56,139 --> 00:57:57,599
This is my first offense.

928
00:57:57,682 --> 00:57:59,976
And I was mentally and physically
impaired due to stress.

929
00:58:00,560 --> 00:58:01,561
Understand what I am.

930
00:58:02,187 --> 00:58:05,899
I'm a doctor, a military doctor, and I
served our country for 20 long years.

931
00:58:06,441 --> 00:58:07,817
The people and the law tend to…

932
00:58:09,068 --> 00:58:11,070
go buck-wild for that sort of story.

933
00:58:13,364 --> 00:58:15,366
Dae-il, you…

934
00:58:17,494 --> 00:58:18,870
will not see light again.

935
00:58:20,371 --> 00:58:23,249
And, yes, you're right,
you'll be in prison for, at most, a year.

936
00:58:23,333 --> 00:58:26,169
And once you're out, by maybe three years
you'll be cleared with the board too,

937
00:58:26,252 --> 00:58:28,171
and you can practice yet again.

938
00:58:28,254 --> 00:58:29,797
Listen to me carefully.

939
00:58:30,757 --> 00:58:33,176
I will do whatever it takes,
with the power that I hold,

940
00:58:33,259 --> 00:58:35,011
with my license on the line,

941
00:58:36,763 --> 00:58:38,806
to have your license
rescinded for eternity.

942
00:58:40,391 --> 00:58:42,018
Because of you,

943
00:58:42,101 --> 00:58:45,438
I had to go against my senses and let
the most dangerous doctor in.

944
00:58:47,565 --> 00:58:51,736
<i>The woman here</i>
<i>flies in the face of authority</i>

945
00:58:51,819 --> 00:58:54,239
<i>and refuses to be bound to anyone.</i>

946
00:58:56,115 --> 00:58:57,158
Dr. Jo.

947
00:58:57,242 --> 00:58:59,327
Dr. Gye Su-jeong wouldn't have
done that, right?

948
00:59:02,789 --> 00:59:03,915
Ask her yourself.

949
00:59:05,208 --> 00:59:07,627
I don't think she would have done
something that twisted.

950
00:59:08,586 --> 00:59:13,091
You're going to pay sorely
and ruinously for that, Dae-il.

951
00:59:17,011 --> 00:59:19,514
Well, Director, perhaps
you'll be the first one to break down.

952
00:59:21,683 --> 00:59:24,018
The next person
coming to visit after you is…

953
00:59:24,602 --> 00:59:26,854
my new lawyer that Magnolia
brought on for my case.

954
00:59:33,903 --> 00:59:35,113
I'm Mun Jeong-ho.

955
00:59:38,658 --> 00:59:40,076
You'll need one too.

956
00:59:40,159 --> 00:59:43,663
I think the person who will actually
bring you and your hospital to its knees

957
00:59:44,581 --> 00:59:46,708
is Gye Su-jeong,
who's in the OR right now.

958
00:59:46,791 --> 00:59:49,627
<i>The weapons in her arsenal</i>
<i>are her medical license</i>

959
00:59:49,711 --> 00:59:52,755
<i>and the surgical skills</i>
<i>she sharpened from bare metal.</i>

960
00:59:52,839 --> 00:59:53,923
Then why are you asking me?

961
00:59:54,674 --> 00:59:55,967
How could I ask her that?

962
00:59:56,634 --> 00:59:57,635
Good lord.

963
00:59:59,220 --> 01:00:03,057
I'm looking forward to watching
how far Gye Su-jeong is gonna take this,

964
01:00:03,141 --> 01:00:07,020
and how long you're able to last.
How many more hits can you take?

965
01:00:22,243 --> 01:00:24,746
PATHOLOGY REPORT
MR. NA DAE-IL

966
01:00:29,792 --> 01:00:31,628
Get out.

967
01:00:31,711 --> 01:00:33,046
You planned all this, didn't you?

968
01:00:33,129 --> 01:00:36,215
You'll have your test results next week.
I can't wait to see them.

969
01:00:36,799 --> 01:00:38,885
Don't worry. I never fail.

970
01:00:40,303 --> 01:00:42,305
So, don't be scared, Na Dae-il.

971
01:00:42,388 --> 01:00:43,848
PATHOLOGY REPORT

972
01:00:43,931 --> 01:00:46,476
RESULTS: BENIGN TUMOR,
NO ABNORMAL FINDINGS

973
01:00:55,526 --> 01:00:57,528
Please, don't.

974
01:01:01,824 --> 01:01:02,867
<i>Listen carefully.</i>

975
01:01:03,785 --> 01:01:07,372
In every hospital, anywhere in Korea,
that woman has a million eyes and ears.

976
01:01:08,081 --> 01:01:11,000
From this day forward,
if you ever get sick or injured,

977
01:01:11,084 --> 01:01:13,419
I will be the one handling your surgery.

978
01:01:14,128 --> 01:01:17,090
No matter which hospital you go to,
or who treats you there,

979
01:01:17,173 --> 01:01:20,593
I will be the one who cuts into you
and stitches you shut.

980
01:01:22,053 --> 01:01:24,389
I'll throw a circus in there
until you're in shreds.

981
01:01:26,140 --> 01:01:27,266
Just so you know.

982
01:01:28,142 --> 01:01:29,936
I have no hesitation in doing so.

983
01:01:35,274 --> 01:01:37,110
Hey! Hey, Gye Su-jeong!

984
01:01:40,321 --> 01:01:42,073
Oh, God! Shit!

985
01:01:44,158 --> 01:01:45,159
Gye Su-jeong!

986
01:01:46,703 --> 01:01:47,954
I mean…

987
01:01:51,165 --> 01:01:53,167
It's not like I went out
and killed anyone, right?

988
01:01:54,544 --> 01:01:56,963
Like, I wasn't out there doing
or dealing drugs or…

989
01:01:57,880 --> 01:02:00,925
or getting hammered ahead of surgery,
so, why? Why?

990
01:02:01,008 --> 01:02:02,468
Why is this happening to me?

991
01:02:04,804 --> 01:02:05,930
Huh?

992
01:02:06,013 --> 01:02:08,307
What did I… What did I do?

993
01:02:08,391 --> 01:02:10,893
What did I…
What did I even do wrong, tell me!

994
01:02:14,105 --> 01:02:15,356
<i>How could I ask her that?</i>

995
01:02:16,274 --> 01:02:18,151
<i>I'm just afraid she might say,</i>

996
01:02:18,901 --> 01:02:20,570
<i>"I did carve something into him."</i>

997
01:02:48,723 --> 01:02:50,850
<i>Gye Su-jeong, general surgeon.</i>

998
01:02:51,392 --> 01:02:53,227
<i>Also known as…</i>

999
01:02:53,853 --> 01:02:55,646
<i>Doctor X.</i>

1000
01:03:35,353 --> 01:03:38,272
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

1001
01:03:38,356 --> 01:03:40,191
<i>There's a surgery we need you to do.</i>

1002
01:03:40,274 --> 01:03:42,735
We want a bullet taken out. Out of here.

1003
01:03:42,819 --> 01:03:45,822
- <i>If she fails though</i>…
<i>- The consequences won't be borne by us.</i>

1004
01:03:45,905 --> 01:03:48,449
They'll rest on the shoulders
of Dr. Gye and Ms. Jang.

1005
01:03:48,533 --> 01:03:50,576
Who's gonna do it? Are you gonna do it?

1006
01:03:50,660 --> 01:03:52,787
Me! I'll perform the surgery.

1007
01:03:52,870 --> 01:03:56,749
He wanted them to see you volunteer,
so they could have someone to blame.

1008
01:03:56,833 --> 01:03:59,710
<i>Failure's a possibility.</i>
<i>If we fail, you will die.</i>

1009
01:03:59,794 --> 01:04:02,797
<i>Are you happy the way you are, though?</i>
<i>Living like this, barely existing?</i>

1010
01:04:02,880 --> 01:04:05,675
<i>What on earth happened that day?</i>
